{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:resolved-private-regimes",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "On the known exact-uniform class \\(\\mathcal M_H\\) and within \\(n^{-1}\\le\\epsilon_n\\le1\\), the bounds match as \\(R_n^{\\mathrm{DP}}\\asymp\\max\\{R_n^{\\mathrm{NP}},\\rho_n^{\\mathrm{priv}}\\}\\) whenever either \\(q\\ge q_0\\) or \\(\\rho_n^{\\mathrm{priv}}\\ge c b_n\\). Under \\(\\epsilon_n=n^{-t}\\), \\(r_F=n^{-(2-t)/D_F}\\) whenever the truncation at one is inactive, and the complete benchmark partition is as follows. If \\(q\\ge q_0\\), privacy is hidden by \\(b_n\\) for \\(0\\le t\\le\\nu\\), and \\(r_G\\) is the leading private branch for \\(t>\\nu\\); at \\(q=q_0\\) and \\(t=\\nu\\), \\(b_n=r_F=r_G\\). If \\(q<q_0\\), privacy is hidden by \\(b_n\\) for \\(0\\le t\\le\\kappa\\), \\(r_F\\) is the leading private branch for \\(\\kappa<t<t_s\\), \\(r_F=r_G\\) at \\(t=t_s=1-q/d-q/\\gamma\\), and \\(r_G\\) is the leading private branch for \\(t>t_s\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "M_H",
      "R_DP",
      "R_NP",
      "rho_priv",
      "q",
      "q_0",
      "b_n",
      "epsilon_n",
